{"translation":{"id":"fra_jnd","name":"Bible J.N. Darby","website":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseUrl":"https://ebible.org/Scriptures/details.php?id=frajnd","licenseNotes":null,"shortName":"JND","englishName":"French: Bible J.N. Darby","language":"fra","textDirection":"ltr","sha256":"121a3f4841e42965f22ebebcf5a8578a12578ec30eaf1ca7ae4e46d5d85ccb80","availableFormats":["json"],"listOfBooksApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/books.json","numberOfBooks":66,"totalNumberOfChapters":1189,"totalNumberOfVerses":31170,"languageName":"français","languageEnglishName":"French"},"book":{"id":"PSA","translationId":"fra_jnd","name":"Les Psaumes","commonName":"Les Psaumes","title":"Les Psaumes","order":19,"numberOfChapters":150,"sha256":"4c48a766d24644f7ef347ae1395ef8ddb5d363cc30acf1733162d22f071b120e","firstChapterNumber":1,"firstChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/1.json","lastChapterNumber":150,"lastChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/150.json","totalNumberOfVerses":2527},"chapter":{"number":76,"content":[{"type":"verse","number":1,"content":[{"text":"Au chef de musique. Sur Neguinoth","poem":1},{"noteId":227},{"text":". Psaume d’Asaph. Cantique.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":2,"content":[{"text":"Dieu est connu en Juda, son nom est grand en Israël ;","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":3,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Et son tabernacle est en Salem, et son domicile en Sion.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":4,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Là, il a brisé les éclairs de l’arc, le bouclier, et l’épée, et la bataille. Sélah.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":5,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Tu es plus resplendissant, plus magnifique que les montagnes de la rapine.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Les forts de cœur ont été dépouillés, ils ont dormi leur sommeil, et aucun des hommes vaillants n’a trouvé ses mains.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Quand tu les as tancés, ô Dieu de Jacob ! chars et chevaux se sont endormis profondément.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Tu es terrible, toi ; et qui est-ce qui subsistera devant toi, dès que ta colère [éclate] ?","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":9,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Tu fis entendre des cieux le jugement ; la terre en eut peur, et se tint tranquille,","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":10,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Quand tu te levas, ô Dieu, pour le jugement, pour sauver tous les débonnaires de la terre","poem":1},{"noteId":228},{"text":". Sélah.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":11,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Car la colère de l’homme te louera ; tu te ceindras du reste de la colère.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":12,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Vouez, et acquittez [vos vœux] envers l’Éternel, votre Dieu ; que tous ceux qui l’entourent apportent des présents au Redoutable.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":13,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Il retranchera l’esprit des princes, il est terrible aux rois de la terre.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":227,"caller":"a","text":"instruments à cordes.","reference":{"chapter":76,"verse":1}},{"noteId":228,"caller":"b","text":"ou : du pays.","reference":{"chapter":76,"verse":10}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/76.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/77.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/fra_jnd/PSA/75.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":13}